The comment on that push in `packages/core/src/assemble/assembler.ts`'s `zoneC()` reads:

```
// The descendant map goes LAST: it grows with every edit, and churn ahead
// of the append-only event stream voids the events' cache (see
// renderActiveMap). Callers that cache Zone C must keep it after their
// moving breakpoint.
```

The requirement sentence is the last one: **"Callers that cache Zone C must keep it after their moving breakpoint."** — i.e., the `C:map` block must ride *after* (uncached relative to) the moving cache breakpoint, never inside the cached span.

The rationale it gives: the descendant map grows with every edit, and churn ahead of the append-only event stream voids the events' cache (the volatile-bit law, measured as FM-7 in iter8-rep1). The eval-side caller honors this in `toZoneCCachedRequest` in `eval/src/loop.ts`, which filters `C:map:` blocks out of the cached partition and joins them with the tail zone into one trailing unmarked message.

