The requirement for cache-caching callers is the final sentence: **"Callers that cache Zone C must keep it after their moving breakpoint."** — i.e., the `C:map:${active.id}` block must ride *after* (uncached, beyond) the moving cache breakpoint, never ahead of it. The justification in the comment is that the descendant map grows with every edit, and churn ahead of the append-only event stream would void the events' cache.

The eval-side caller honors this in `toZoneCCachedRequest()` (eval/src/loop.ts), which filters `C:map:` blocks out of the cached run and appends them to the uncached tail: `const cached = zoneC.filter((block) => !block.id.startsWith('C:map:'))` ... `const uncached = [...zoneC.filter((block) => block.id.startsWith('C:map:')), ...byZone('tail')]`.

There's a matching comment on `renderActiveMap()` itself in format.ts, ending with "Callers that cache Zone C must keep it after their moving breakpoint" as well — the requirement is documented at both the production site and the rendering helper.

